// once elements are aliasable/counted, the same class of bug ARC Task 4's
// Bug 2 fixed for named slots. Args: (list, index, new value) -- cprint's
// shared printer computes the list/index ONCE and reuses both C strings for
// the old-element read+release AND the new-element write, so an
// index expression with a side effect is never evaluated twice. IListSet is
// the birth/transfer form (no retain); IListSetRetain additionally retains
// the new value BEFORE reading/releasing the old one (self-overwrite safety
// -- `lst[i] = lst[i]`: retaining first guarantees the shared handle's rc
// never transiently reaches zero from the old-element release that follows).
