// IUiEdit (mac-target-4d Task 7, Ch10's Edit Statement) is `edit F, target`
// (or `edit F, new T`) -- always a bare statement (SExprStmt wrapping this
// Intr), never assigned, so its own `ty` is hijacked to carry the form
// window's name (irWinRefType(winName), the same "ty carries the payload,
// not just the C type" trick IUiOpen/IUiFront already use for their own
// window-name lookup) rather than a real return type. args: a0 is an
// IntConst tag (0=`new T`, 1=RT_UI_WB_ADDR, 2=RT_UI_WB_LIST, 3=RT_UI_WB_MAP
// -- deliberately the SAME numbers rt_ui.h's own RT_UI_WB_* use, since 1-3
// map straight through and 0 doubles as WB_NONE's value for the `new T`
// case); a1/a2 (kind 1: lvalue, -; kind 2: list, index; kind 3: map, key)
// are already-lowered IR exprs, -1/absent for kind 0. See cprint.cla's
// fpUiEditStmt for the four call shapes this decodes into.
